  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Soaking rain early this morning to help with \nongoing drought conditions.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION... \nAs of 2am Thursday, a broad low pressure system in northern \nCanada is bringing a strong warm front through our area, with\nwidespread rain. Rain will end abruptly from west to east 4-7am.\nTotals will end up being generally one third to one inch, with\nmost of that coming in 4-6 hours. The least amount of rain\n(around one third of an inch) looks to come in the St John\nValley. Flooding is not a concern with this system, but rain \namounts should give some relief to the ongoing D1-D2 drought \nconditions. After the system exits around or a bit before dawn, \nscattered showers are still possible over the north, but areas \nsouth of Millinocket should be dry today.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Strong gusty winds during the day today and \nFriday. Cannot rule out isolated power outages.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION... As mentioned above, strong low \npressure system passes to the north of the forecast area, with \nstrong winds aloft. This will bring strong winds during the day\ntoday from the west, and again from the west/northwest during \nthe day Friday. Gusts potentially up to 35 mph today and 30 mph\nFriday. With wet soils after tonights rain, plus leaves on the \ntrees, there could be very isolated tree damage/power outages\ntoday.",
